COMMUNICATION UART - VARIANT_USART

UART1: ARDUINO <-> MASTER

Arduino => Master: SerialUart1 (CONTROL_SERIAL_USART1)
    start
    enableMotors
    controlMode
    speedMaster
    speedSlave
    checksum

Master => Arduino: SerialFeedback (FEEDBACK_SERIAL_USART1)
    start
    cmd1                    // command input 1
    cmd2                    // command input 2
    speedMaster_meas        // measured speed of Master motor
    speedSlave_meas         // measured speed received from Slave
    batVoltage
    boardTempMaster
    boardTempSlave
    enableFinMaster
    enableFinSlave
    chargeStatus
    motor_dc_currMaster     // Master current * 100
    motor_dc_currSlave      // Slave current * 100
    cmdLed
    checksum


UART2: MASTER <-> SLAVE

Both directions use SerialUart2 / SerialSend_Usart2. The frame has the
same field order in both directions; fields not owned by the sender are
sent as zero.

Master => Slave:
    start
    enableMotors
    controlMode
    speedMaster = 0
    speedSlave
    speedSlave_meas = 0
    bateryVoltage
    boardTemp             // Master board temperature
    errCode               // Master error code
    enableFin = 0
    chargeStatus
    cmdLed
    motor_dc_curr         // Master current * 100
    checksum

Slave => Master:
    start
    enableMotors = 0
    controlMode = 0
    speedMaster = 0
    speedSlave = 0
    speedSlave_meas       // Slave measured speed
    bateryVoltage = 0
    boardTemp             // Slave board temperature
    errCode               // Slave error code
    enableFin              // Slave enable feedback
    chargeStatus = 0
    cmdLed = 0
    motor_dc_curr         // Slave current * 100
    checksum

The Master combines the UART2 data into UART1 feedback:
    motor_dc_currMaster = local Master current
    motor_dc_currSlave  = motor_dc_curr received from Slave
